<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3958] Client node should not start rest processor</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3958</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description></description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13007092">IGNITE-3958</key>
            <summary>Client node should not start rest processor</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
                                            <priority id="3" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/priorities/major.svg">Major</priority>
                        <status id="5" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/resolved.png" description="A resolution has been taken, and it is awaiting verification by reporter. From here issues are either reopened, or are closed.">Resolved</status>
                    <statusCategory id="3" key="done" colorName="green"/>
                                    <resolution id="1">Fixed</resolution>
                                        <assignee username="ntikhonov">Nikolay Tikhonov</assignee>
                                    <reporter username="yzhdanov">Yakov Zhdanov</reporter>
                        <labels>
                    </labels>
                <created>Fri, 23 Sep 2016 08:50:53 +0000</created>
                <updated>Thu, 24 Nov 2016 12:40:21 +0000</updated>
                            <resolved>Thu, 24 Nov 2016 12:40:20 +0000</resolved>
                                                    <fixVersion>2.0</fixVersion>
                                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>5</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15522492" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 26 Sep 2016 08:51:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Why client should not start REST processor? Looks weird to me. This is normal use case to use client nodes as a gateway for various external activities. E.g. to listen for ODBC requests and start queries, collect data for web-console, start tasks for REST, etc..&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15524945" author="vkulichenko" created="Tue, 27 Sep 2016 03:36:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Agree. But I think that management endpoints (e.g. for Visor) should only be started on servers.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15524983" author="kuaw26" created="Tue, 27 Sep 2016 03:59:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Val, why?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client node may be a kind of &quot;gateway&quot; for private cluster.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15525176" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 27 Sep 2016 05:59:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+1 to Alex question. I do not quite understand how management endpoint is different from any other client gateways? &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15525188" author="vkulichenko" created="Tue, 27 Sep 2016 06:05:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Also a good point. Actually, I don&apos;t think it&apos;s a very common use case and a regular user would expect that REST will connect to server nodes. Having said that, ideally REST should be disabled on clients by default with an option to enable it. But this is an incompatible change, so probably it&apos;s better to do it in 2.0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=yzhdanov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;yzhdanov&quot;&gt;yzhdanov&lt;/a&gt;, can you chime in?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15671371" author="ntikhonov" created="Wed, 16 Nov 2016 19:31:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Guys,&lt;br/&gt;
I&apos;ve implemented the following approach (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1240):&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1240):&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;By default REST processor does not start on clinet nodes;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;For start REST processor on client node need to add envirement property IGNITE_REST_START_ON_CLIENT;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When REST processor does not start on client in logs prints message &quot;REST protocols have not been started. For start the protocols on a client node add -DIGNITE_REST_START_ON_CLIENT=true&quot;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
